WEBVTT

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.300
<i>I shot...</i>

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>Ryo...</i>

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.390
Ukai!

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.470
Ango!

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.690
Damn! I can't aim with my left hand.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.650
<i>I am setting the missile launch
and self-denotation of this ship</i>

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.190
<i>to commence in 24 hours.</i>

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.410
LESSER COLD

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.000
<i>I didn't mean to pull the trigger.</i>

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.540
<i>It just happened.</i>

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.710
<i>The recoil was so powerful.</i>

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.540
<i>I can't breathe.</i>

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:17.970
<i>Mom, I swore I would never
get involved with drugs or guns.</i>

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:20.800
<i>What happened to Ryo?</i>

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.760
What the hell are you doing?

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.520
Are you playing dumb
while trying to kill me?

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.890
<i>I was the one who got shot?</i>

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.150
<i>What a relief, Mom.
I'm so glad I didn't shoot anyone.</i>

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.280
<i>I feel much better this way.</i>

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.450
What's going on? What happened?

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.450
Semmy! Hang in there! Don't die on us!

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.950
Isn't that a bulletproof vest?

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.950
What?

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.750
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.250
A missile launch?

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.460
That will rain down on all of Japan?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.500
What is that captain saying?

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.380
Should we watch it one more time?

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.510
No, that's not necessary.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.300
Well, there's no reason for us to panic.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.100
This was from a very long time ago.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.680
But I'm curious as to
what happened afterwards.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.270
Then what do you suppose
these numbers mean?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.350
Perhaps, for some reason,

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:19.320
the countdown was canceled after that
and has now started back up again?

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.780
<i>Which means that,
when this number reaches zero...</i>

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.080
That's assuming the devices on the ship
are still working properly.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.160
That's a good point.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.290
It's all broken down.
I doubt it will work.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.880
But we should probably still
go ahead and stop it anyway.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.010
Where was the control room?

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:42.010
Right now,
it's at the very top of the ship.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.680
Let's go.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.930
He said that one of the missiles was
a nuke, didn't he?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.890
Japan wasn't supposed to have any nukes.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.150
When everyone realized
that humanity was doomed,

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:04.570
their conscience and concept of adhering
to the rules must have crumbled.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.540
I'm sure they thought everyone
left in the world would fight over food

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.460
and come to attack Japan.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.500
Which is why they left weapons behind.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.880
And ended up killing their compatriots.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.300
They had the same idea.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.670
What?

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.420
Nothing, forget it.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:29.760
<i>I was given this neurotoxin
to kill ourselves if worse comes to worst.</i>

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.600
<i>To bravely die together beautifully,
apparently.</i>

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.610
<i>That's an idea that probably
only the Japanese have.</i>

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:40.860
<i>What beauty is there in that?</i>

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.280
Arashi!

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.450
Did I actually shoot at you?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.830
It's my fault for calling out to you
with no warning.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.920
No, it was my mistake.

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.420
<i>Was I hallucinating?</i>

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.710
We have more important things
to worry about.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.550
Right.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:09.800
No good.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.730
But if the water keeps flowing out here,
it should drain eventually, right?

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.020
Yes.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.770
<i>Why was I hallucinating?</i>

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.150
Ryo?

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.290
The floor is higher on the other side.
This side will fill up first.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.870
Arashi, do you have your knife?

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:37.290
Yes.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.920
I kept it with me, just like you said.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.500
We'll remove this wire mesh.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:41.920
Help me. Hurry!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.050
Right!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.100
Let's move!

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.100
Right!

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.270
The water has stopped.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.940
This is a giant water tank.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.650
If we had stayed in that room...

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.690
It would have completely flooded.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.700
Thanks for your help.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.160
<i>"Thanks"? That's not right.</i>

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.330
<i>I caused that mess in the first place.</i>

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:19.540
Boy, it's cold. It's really cold.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.250
The water was freezing.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.250
Strip.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.510
What?

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.100
<i>This is warm...</i>

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:38.020
<i>I think I should ask him
why he's carrying a gun.</i>

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.520
<i>But I'm certain
there must be a reason for it.</i>

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:46.030
<i>If I'm starting to hallucinate,
then I'm totally worthless.</i>

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.530
<i>I thought I was walking through a cave,
trying to find Shigeru.</i>

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.450
<i>I thought Arashi was Ukai.</i>

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:00.920
<i>I tried to shoot him with my gun,
Hana's boyfriend.</i>

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:03.920
<i>I'm the one who killed Hana.</i>

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:08.670
<i>Maybe it would be best if I shot
this guy too and was done with it.</i>

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.100
<i>His guard is totally down,</i>

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.560
<i>even though he's with a guy
who just shot at him.</i>

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.440
<i>I don't think we can climb this.</i>

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.400
<i>Even if we went back through the water,
the exit is blocked.</i>

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.650
<i>What the hell am I doing?</i>

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:33.820
Ango...

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.200
Semmy!

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.290
I don't see any broken bones.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.000
Maybe you just got a bad bruise?

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.620
Consider yourself lucky
if that's the worst of it.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.330
I thought I had died.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.170
Tell me, why did you aim at--

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.880
There's something here!

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.970
There's something dangerous
inside this ship!

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.390
<i>Okay, I'm going to do this.</i>

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.730
<i>I'll climb the ladder, cross the beam,
and reach the door up there.</i>

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.980
Just stay in here, Mimi.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:11.990
<i>I have to make my own decisions
and take responsibility for them.</i>

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.240
<i>Nobody is watching now,
so nobody will laugh or get angry with me.</i>

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.290
<i>I'm going to do this.</i>

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:22.000
<i>Please don't let this be a mistake.</i>

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.250
So, this ship is still floating stably.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.880
Yes. It just rotated vertically.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.800
It seems like it was meant to.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:34.630
A turtle?

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.470
They were likely keeping it
in this tank for food.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.230
In the Age of Exploration,
they often kept giant tortoises on ships.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.730
They are easy to care for and eat little
but are very meaty.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.440
Oh, I think I've heard that before.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.360
That's how they ended up
being driven to extinction.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.780
But this is seawater, isn't it?

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:58.200
They must have chosen a sea turtle
since they have easy access to seawater.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.700
You know a lot, Ango.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:06.250
These turtles don't seem like
they're dead, though.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.290
They might be in hibernation.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.920
Hibernation?

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.260
<i>How long have they been asleep?</i>

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.260
<i>Did they travel through time
just like we did?</i>

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.640
It's incredible
that they can do that all by themselves.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:26.020
If they ever wake back up, I'd like to
release them into the sea or at the beach.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.400
It's possible that they could thrive here.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.360
If this ship doesn't sink
and we can use it,

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:35.190
we might also raise the turtles here
for food.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.820
On this ship...

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:42.910
Ango, to be honest, I felt something odd
when I came on this ship.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.500
It has electricity and is similar to
what our world used to be like,

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.590
yet it didn't make me
feel nostalgic at all.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.210
I thought that, even if this ship was
safe and in perfect condition,

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:56.420
I wouldn't want to live
my life on board it.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:02.430
There's this thing
my girlfriend used to say.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.440
<i>A starry night sky
and the flames of a campfire.</i>

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:10.810
I don't think
there's anything more comforting in life.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.690
But, when she said that,

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:18.110
I blurted out, "It can't be comforting
with a bunch of bugs crawling around!"

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.950
However, I understand her
a little better now.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:26.870
<i>Everyone gathered around the campfire.</i>

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:30.330
<i>The slow passing of the evening hours.</i>

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.880
<i>Bathing in the morning sun,
feeling your body charged by its energy.</i>

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.920
All of those things
have become comforting to me.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:43.640
<i>I want to tell Hana this
as we sit by the campfire.</i>

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.520
Don't you feel that way at all, Ango?

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:51.480
<i>That girlfriend must be Hana.</i>

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.610
<i>We light a campfire
because it's necessary to survive.</i>

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.700
<i>The stars are for finding directions
and predicting the weather.</i>

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.070
<i>The morning sun is simply
a sign to remind you</i>

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.120
<i>that you survived the night
and another day has begun.</i>

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.790
<i>Hana is already dead.</i>

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.210
Arashi, the truth is, your girlfriend--

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:15.460
Ango, look up there.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.460
Is that Natsu?

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.930
<i>Just a little farther.</i>

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:27.520
<i>It's not as thin as a balance beam,
so it's tempting to hurry across it.</i>

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.180
<i>But I can't forget this is a ship.</i>

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.650
<i>It might sway at any time.</i>

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.730
<i>Not too long ago, there was a loud noise
from below and I felt a tremor.</i>

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:39.440
<i>So I won't rush.</i>

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:42.530
<i>I will go slowly until I reach that door.</i>

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.280
Natsu?

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.950
What are you doing? Don't!

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.280
Hey, Ango.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:48.990
We shouldn't call out to her now.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:52.080
It's best not to break her focus
by calling attention to us.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:53.670
She can't...

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:55.290
She'll fall.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.250
Just stop.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.710
That's not going to happen, Ango.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.630
Natsu is a very cautious person.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.050
She doesn't get desperate, or risk things,
or act carelessly.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.050
That's not the type of person she is.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.180
I don't know what happened,

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:12.180
but she wouldn't try to cross
unless she thought she could.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.100
So she's going to be fine.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:15.560
No.

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.650
<i>She'll fall.</i>

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.230
Natsu!

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.200
<i>Did someone say my name?
Or did I imagine it?</i>

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:28.490
<i>I'm too scared to look down.</i>

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.910
<i>Water? Is that water down there?</i>

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.580
<i>Then if I fall...</i>

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.170
<i>No, I'm still way too high up.</i>

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:42.210
Ango!

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:46.260
Amazing.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.890
Natsu! Stop! What are you doing? Go back!

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:54.140
You don't have a lifeline, do you?
Don't be reckless!

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:57.060
Ango?

00:12:57.150 --> 00:13:00.320
Damn, I told you!
Now she's become all unsteady!

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.570
I did it.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.240
Natsu! Just stay calm!

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.120
Arashi?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.620
Yes! It's me!

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.290
I'm sorry I went out on my own!

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:19.380
I got washed away by the current,
but this is where I ended up.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.760
I realize that I caused everyone
a lot of worry and concern!

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.220
I'm sorry!

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:28.300
How have you been?

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:29.850
Are you okay right now?

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.060
Natsu.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.270
I'm so glad to see you again.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.520
Is there anyone else up there with you?

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.520
No, I'm on my own!

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:43.360
Okay, then listen well!

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:45.900
We're stuck down here!

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.410
The way we came is blocked,
so we can't go back!

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:50.570
I think our only option is to climb up!

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:52.700
Do you know a way we can do that?

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.540
Is there any rope or anything close by?

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:57.790
What?

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:01.380
Arashi! Don't make Natsu do that.
It's impossible!

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.590
No, it's not!

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.300
Ango, just be quiet for a moment!

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:08.130
Natsu! I'm sure you're scared,
but just stay calm!

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:09.800
Focus and think!

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:13.810
Find a way to get us out of here!
We need you!

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.140
Natsu!

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.350
Help them?

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:20.730
I can do something to help them both?

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.650
It's impossible. She can't do it.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.490
Ango, why are you so insistent about that?

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:29.360
Natsu is very patient
and has a strong sense of responsibility.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.530
She's worked very hard to make it this far
without ever complaining.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:34.870
I've always relied on her.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:39.750
Ango?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.420
I'm going to save you no matter what.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.960
<i>What exactly can I do to help those two?</i>

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:50.470
<i>I have to think on my own,
without being given any orders.</i>

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:52.680
<i>But if I fail...</i>

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.100
<i>I can't waste time thinking like that.</i>

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:04.650
<i>I have to save them!
There's no one else here to do it!</i>

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:09.780
<i>If our roles were reversed,
I know for sure that they would help me.</i>

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.200
<i>So I want to help them.</i>

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.990
<i>I want to save both of them!</i>

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:18.040
<i>Instead of always being saved,</i>

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:22.290
<i>I want to become someone useful,
someone who helps others.</i>

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.130
<i>How many meters to the bottom, I wonder?</i>

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:29.670
<i>I'm pretty high up.</i>

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.130
<i>I don't think
I'm capable of pulling them up here.</i>

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:37.060
<i>And Ango's right arm is injured,
so he can't climb up on his own.</i>

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:42.560
<i>If only there was a long ladder
or a rope ladder, even something sturdy.</i>

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.270
<i>But there's nothing...</i>

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:49.530
A crane!

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.860
<i>I see! This beam is designed
for use with a crane.</i>

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.620
<i>But how can I get it to move?</i>

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.290
<i>In fact, is it even still working?</i>

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:01.790
<i>That's it.</i>

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.290
<i>I can't reach it.</i>

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:07.170
What are you doing?

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.250
<i>Natsu...</i>

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:12.930
<i>That means I need to backtrack</i>

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.890
<i>and go down to the controller
to operate it.</i>

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:19.010
<i>Go back...</i>

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.400
Arashi! Ango!

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:26.940
What is it?

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:30.110
I'm going to see if I can get
this crane to work!

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.030
Please hold on a bit!

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:35.910
Roger that! Just be careful!
Take all the time you need!

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.200
<i>Even changing directions
is pretty scary up here.</i>

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.170
Okay, let's do this.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:53.920
<i>When I first came to this world,
I couldn't even shout when I needed to.</i>

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.430
<i>I still can't without a little courage.</i>

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:58.930
<i>But...</i>

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.020
<i>Please work.</i>

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:07.650
It's working! We can use it!

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.940
Now to position it.
A little more to the right.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:13.530
Oh, I went too far.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.290
I'm going to lower the crane to you!

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:35.720
Okay! Stop it!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.180
Raise it when I give the signal!

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.220
Okay, I will!

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.310
Let's go. Have some faith in Natsu.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.770
I hope the cable doesn't snap
while they're on it...

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.020
or the beam doesn't break.

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:55.490
No, I can't let myself think about
things going wrong.

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:57.570
Okay! Bring us up!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:17:59.320
All right!

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.170
Mission complete, Natsu!

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:23.600
Natsu.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:24.970
What...

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.600
It's fine! Just jump!

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.940
Thanks so much, Natsu!

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:38.450
You saved our lives.

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.030
I was hoping we would meet again!

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.200
Give me ten.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:51.000
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:56.920
<i>What is this bad feeling
that I can't shake?</i>

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:00.220
<i>I think it said we had 13 hours left.</i>

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:02.300
PROCESS CAN BE CANCELLED
WITHIN THE FIRST 12 HOURS.

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.470
LESS THAN 30 MINUTES REMAIN.

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:05.510
There were jellyfish that gave off heat.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:09.690
But I was cold and scared,
and I missed everyone so much.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.100
Oh, we found some turtles here earlier.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:16.110
I only found a bunch of skeletons.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:20.820
But if you hadn't found us,
we would've been stuck down there.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:22.610
Right, Ango?

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.080
It hurts!

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:37.420
Don't leave behind stupid shit like this!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.260
People might use them if you do!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:42.220
If people accidentally use them,
they cause trouble, and it hurts!

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:43.430
Damn it!

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.390
We don't need junk like this!

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:49.270
We just end up shooting our friends,
even though we don't want to!

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.480
They should have left us
something more useful!

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:55.020
You know, like food, or food,
or supplies, or some damn food!

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:59.400
Guns just aren't cool at all, damn it!

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:02.070
You thought they were cool?

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.990
Ango... He's pretty far down.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.540
"Together with Natsu and Arashi."

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.410
-Arashi?
-Arashi?

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.790
Arashi is here? Yes! That's great news!

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:16.380
"Found turtles."

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:17.590
Turtles?

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:20.260
<i>Does he really have his head on straight?</i>

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.220
<i>I want to change my napkin.</i>

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:30.220
<i>A bathroom!</i>

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:31.680
Oh, the bathroom?

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:33.520
Do you think it even works?

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.520
Oh, well...

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.810
I just need some privacy for a minute.

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:39.230
Sorry.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:21.400
<i>There's plenty of water.</i>

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.820
<i>But I won't drink it directly.
I'll boil it first.</i>

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:31.490
<i>There are so many animals here.</i>

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:34.290
<i>They must have all known about this spot.</i>

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.460
<i>Thanks for showing me the way.</i>

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:40.420
<i>I can't believe there are so many.</i>

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:44.340
<i>When I first awoke here,
I thought there weren't any mammals left.</i>

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:49.760
<i>But they survived
and I'm sure there are even more.</i>

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:54.430
<i>They made it through
the natural disaster alive somehow...</i>

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.390
<i>and have survived.</i>

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:01.770
Look, there are some animals around here
that might be like you.

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:06.110
I wonder if
any of the other teams are here.

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:09.410
Maybe even Arashi came here.

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:14.450
What? What's wrong?

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:18.540
Wait! If there's water, then that means...
